From freebsd-alpha  Wed Jul 21 08:41:55 1999
From: Doug Rabson <dfr () nlsystems ! com>
Date: Wed, 21 Jul 1999 08:41:55 +0000
To: freebsd-alpha
Subject: Re: kern/12378
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=freebsd-alpha&m=103030573207875

On Wed, 21 Jul 1999, Alan Cox wrote:

> Could one of you take a look at PR kern/12378?  Specifically, I'd
> like a confirmation that the same pmap change should be applied
> to the Alpha as well as the x86.

The same problem potentially exists in the alpha if the kernel VM space
overflows grows such that a new level 2 page table is needed (as you know,
the alpha uses 3 levels of page tables and if a level 3 page table is
added, nothing special needs to happen since the corresponding level 2
page table is already shared by all processes).

The suggested fix looks as if it could be easily adapted to the alpha
pmap.

