> Mmm 4T interesting...
> My Documentation says that my 21066 is limited to 43Bit Vitual - which should
> be something around 4T
> Applys the 43Bit limit to modern alpha CPUs too or is FreeBSD limiting.

I think 21264s can use larger address spaces but FreeBSD is currently
limited to 43bit virtual (half for user, quarter for direct map
physical->virtual and quarter for pte mapped kernel).

Supporting 53bit addressing wouldn't be very hard. The main different is
that it needs four levels of pagetables instead of three.

